{"name":"Marsh Creek","hex":"#6b8781","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marsh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area of low, wet land, often with tall grass or herbaceous plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marsh"},{"term":"creek","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small inlet, often saltwater, leading to the sea or to the main channel of a river, especially a river estuary.","The inner part of a port that is used as a dock for small boats."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creek"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marsh Creek (California)","blocks":[{"text":"Marsh Creek is a stream in east Contra Costa County, California in Northern California which rises on the eastern side of Mount Diablo and flows 30 miles (48 km) to the Sacramento–San Joaquin River Delta at Oakley, California, near Big Break Regional Shoreline. The creek flows through Marsh Creek State Park, where water is impounded to form Marsh Creek Reservoir, then through the city of Brentwood, California."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Marsh_Creek_Reservoir.jpg/330px-Marsh_Creek_Reservoir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsh_Creek_(California)","wikidata":"Q6773306"},{"title":"Marsh Creek (Missouri)","blocks":[{"text":"Marsh Creek is a stream in Madison County in the U.S. state of Missouri. It is a tributary of the St. Francis River."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsh_Creek_(Missouri)","wikidata":"Q27985637"},{"title":"Marsh","blocks":[{"text":"In ecology, a marsh is a wetland that is dominated by herbaceous plants rather than by woody plants. More in general, the word can be used for any low-lying and seasonally waterlogged terrain. In Europe and in agricultural literature, low-lying meadows that require draining and embanked polderlands are also referred to as marshes or marshland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg/330px-Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsh","wikidata":"Q30198"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Coastal_marsh_profile.png/500px-Coastal_marsh_profile.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Coastal_marsh_profile.png/500px-Coastal_marsh_profile.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marsh in shallow water on a lakeshore","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoastal_marsh_profile.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg/500px-Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg/500px-Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"White water lilies are a typical marsh plant in European areas of deeper water.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWater_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg/500px-Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg/500px-Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u